{#
settings/_compose_defaults_chips.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
One Always Bcc list as chips (#692): a <select multiple> of the stored
addresses that settings--address-chips turns into a Tom Select with the
composer's contact suggestions, and that saves on every chip. Without
JavaScript it is a plain multi-select of what is stored, and its Save button
posts it unchanged — the field needs the widget to add anything.

Variables:
  id           the <select>'s id; Tom Select names its input "<id>-ts-control"
  action       the route it posts to
  token        its CSRF token
  addresses    list<string>, what is stored
  placeholder  what the input says
  empty        optional: what it says instead while the list is empty
  label        the accessible name
  i18n         JSON: {create, noResults, add}
#}
<form method="post" action="{{ action }}"
      data-turbo-stream
      data-controller="settings--address-chips"
      data-settings--address-chips-url-value="{{ path('app_contacts_autocomplete_recipients') }}"
      data-settings--address-chips-i18n-value="{{ i18n }}"
      data-settings--address-chips-empty-value="{{ empty ?? '' }}"
      class="mt-1.5">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ token }}">
    <select id="{{ id }}" name="addresses[]" multiple
            aria-label="{{ label }}"
            placeholder="{{ placeholder }}"
            class="w-full">
        {% for address in addresses %}
            <option value="{{ address }}" selected>{{ address }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
    </select>
    <noscript>
        <button type="submit" class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.compose_defaults.bcc.save'|trans }}</button>
    </noscript>
</form>
